+# S004 Data model: provider retry quota
+
+## Purpose
+
+This logical model gives each reminder send attempt one durable reservation so retry credits can be settled exactly once. It is storage-neutral because the workspace has no source or database evidence.
+
+## Entities
+
+### WorkspaceRetryQuota
+
+| Field | Meaning | Rules |
+|-------|---------|-------|
+| `workspace_id` | Workspace that owns the retry credits. | Primary identity; must match its reservations. |
+| `available_retry_credits` | Credits that may still be reserved. | Integer; never less than zero. |
+| `updated_at` | Last durable change to the quota. | Written with each reserve or restore. |
+
+### RetryCreditReservation
+
+| Field | Meaning | Rules |
+|-------|---------|-------|
+| `reservation_id` | Durable identifier carried through the dispatch lifecycle. | Unique. |
+| `workspace_id` | Workspace whose credit is reserved. | Must reference the same workspace as the quota row. |
+| `attempt_id` | Stable identifier for one reminder send attempt. | Unique per workspace; repeat reserve calls find this record. |
+| `state` | `reserved`, `finalized`, or `restored`. | Starts as `reserved`; terminal states never change. |
+| `reserved_at` | Time the credit was reserved. | Required. |
+| `settled_at` | Time the record reached a terminal state. | Required only for terminal states. |
+| `settlement_reason` | `accepted`, `provider_failed`, `timeout`, or `cancelled`. | Required for terminal states; `accepted` only with `finalized`. |
+
+## Relationships
+
+- One `WorkspaceRetryQuota` has many `RetryCreditReservation` records.
+- One logical `(workspace_id, attempt_id)` has at most one reservation.
+
+## State transitions
+
+| Current state | Command | Next state | Balance effect |
+|---------------|---------|------------|----------------|
+| none | reserve with available credit | `reserved` | decrement by one in the same atomic operation |
+| none | reserve without available credit | none | no change |
+| `reserved` | finalize accepted send | `finalized` | no change |
+| `reserved` | restore failure, timeout, or cancellation | `restored` | increment by one in the same atomic operation |
+| `finalized` or `restored` | any duplicate terminal command | unchanged | no change |
+
+## Invariants
+
+1. `available_retry_credits >= 0` at every committed state.
+2. A reservation is created only with the same atomic operation that decrements the quota.
+3. A restore increments the quota only when it changes a matching reservation from `reserved` to `restored`.
+4. A finalization changes a matching reservation only from `reserved` to `finalized`.
+5. A terminal reservation cannot be settled again, regardless of duplicate provider callbacks.
+6. No terminal operation may settle a reservation for a different workspace.
+
+## Persistence requirements
+
+The implementation must use the repository’s existing transaction, conditional update, or compare-and-set primitive. The aggregate quota update and the corresponding reservation mutation share one atomic boundary on reserve and restore. The uniqueness guarantee on `(workspace_id, attempt_id)` is required for retry-safe reserve behavior.
